<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Evaluation results (mIoU, %) on six <span id="S6.T4.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">semantic segmentation benchmarks</span>. Our results are marked in <span id="S6.T4.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">gray</span>. <span id="S6.T4.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">LazyStrike</span> consistently improves semantic segmentation results under text supervision across different type of CLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> and model sizes, demonstrating that, after understanding the essence of the problem, a simple approach can uniformly address issues across different models.</figcaption>
</figure>
